# Cursor co-author gate

If the work is agent-driven or the commit will include `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, **do not declare done** until all of the following hold:

## Run vibe-ship invariants (mandatory — not optional / not “steward later”)

**Execute** these commands in the agent session and fix failures before claiming done.
Branch protection may be unavailable; that does **not** waive this gate.

```bash
npm run check:vibe-ship
npm run check:god-components
```

## Blocking (correctness)

- [ ] Change checklist (`change-checklist.mdc`) satisfied
- [ ] No dual SSOT / legacy process clients for pots touched
- [ ] Identity keys are IDs (`user_id`), not display names
- [ ] Backend companion implications acknowledged (or landed)
- [ ] Vibe-ship invariant commands above were **run** and **passed** in this session

## Blocking (hygiene)

- [ ] File-size / god-component ceilings still pass (or this change splits the offender)
- [ ] New projection/window/fund helpers have unit tests
- [ ] E2E mocks/fixtures updated for new APIs
- [ ] Commits are partitioned (see `commit-cadence.mdc` / `agent-commit-partition.mdc`)

## Steward follow-ups

List follow-ups **only** for non-blocking polish.

**Never** mark dual clients, wrong counting/windows, broken imports, or **failing vibe-ship invariants** as “non-blocking follow-up.”
